# A recording platform adapter for shared-engine tests; never imported by applications.
import ../../ui/application.dl

class:
    patterns:
        test UI surface
    members:
        paints as an integer
        wakes as an integer
        copied as a string
        drawn as a string
        cursor as an integer

to open test UI {a pointer to UI view:view} sized {integer:width} by {integer:height} titled {C string:title}:
    set surface to a new test UI surface
    set view's window to (storage for one slot initialized with surface) as a pointer

to close test UI {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    destroy the value at (view's window as a pointer to test UI surface)
    deallocate (view's window as a pointer to test UI surface)

to poll test UI {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    ignore view

to begin test UI {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    set surface to view's window as a pointer to test UI surface
    set surface's drawn to ""
    set view's drawable to true

to present test UI {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    set surface to view's window as a pointer to test UI surface
    increment surface's paints

to submit test UI {a pointer to UI view:view} vertices {a pointer to UI vertex:vertices} counting {integer:count} with {a pointer:texture}:
    require condition ((count > 0) and ((count mod 3) = 0)) reporting "The renderer emitted incomplete triangles"
    set index to 0
    loop while index < count:
        set vertex to the item at index in vertices
        require condition ((vertex's x is finite) and (vertex's y is finite)) reporting "The renderer emitted invalid geometry"
        require condition ((vertex's alpha >= 0.0) and (vertex's alpha <= 1.0)) reporting "The renderer emitted invalid coverage"
        increment index

to get a test UI font in {a pointer to UI view:view} from {C string:path} sized {integer:size}:
    return 1 as a pointer

to release test UI font {a pointer:resource}:
    ignore resource

to get the test UI [width] of {a pointer:resource} containing {C string:text} counting {integer:count}:
    set content to a new string from text containing count bytes
    set index to 0
    set width to 0.0
    loop while index < count:
        set character to the UTF8 character at index in content
        require condition (character's valid) reporting "Invalid test text"
        set index to character's next
        set width to width + 8.0
    return width

to draw test UI text in {a pointer to UI view:view} using {a pointer:font} containing {C string:text} counting {integer:count} at {floating-point number:x} {floating-point number:y} in {a pointer to UI paint:ink}:
    set surface to view's window as a pointer to test UI surface
    set surface's drawn to (surface's drawn + (a new string from text containing count bytes)) + "\n"

to get the test UI icon in {a pointer to UI view:view} from {a pointer to UI SVG icon:icon} sized {integer:size}:
    return 1 as a pointer

to release test UI texture in {a pointer to UI view:view} holding {a pointer:texture}:
    ignore texture

to copy test UI text in {a pointer to UI view:view} containing {C string:text} counting {integer:count}:
    set surface to view's window as a pointer to test UI surface
    set surface's copied to the substring of (a new string from text containing count bytes) from 0 spanning count bytes

to launch test UI {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    ignore view

to wake test UI {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    set surface to view's window as a pointer to test UI surface
    increment surface's wakes

the test UI driver means: a static reference to @intrinsic("construct", UI driver, (the function named "open test UI $ sized $ by $ titled $") as a pointer, (the function named "close test UI $") as a pointer, (the function named "poll test UI $") as a pointer, (the function named "begin test UI $") as a pointer, (the function named "present test UI $") as a pointer, (the function named "submit test UI $ vertices $ counting $ with $") as a pointer, (the function named "a test UI font in $ from $ sized $") as a pointer, (the function named "release test UI font $") as a pointer, (the function named "the test UI width of $ containing $ counting $") as a pointer, (the function named "draw test UI text in $ using $ containing $ counting $ at $ $ in $") as a pointer, (the function named "the test UI icon in $ from $ sized $") as a pointer, (the function named "release test UI texture in $ holding $") as a pointer, (the function named "copy test UI text in $ containing $ counting $") as a pointer, (the function named "launch test UI $") as a pointer, (the function named "wake test UI $") as a pointer, (the function named "set test UI cursor in $ to $") as a pointer)

to set test UI cursor in {a pointer to UI view:view} to {integer:shape}:
    set surface to view's window as a pointer to test UI surface
    set surface's cursor to shape
